# =============================================================================
# CLIENT ENVIRONMENT (Vite)
# =============================================================================
# Only VITE_-prefixed variables reach the browser bundle. Never put a secret
# here — anything with a VITE_ prefix is public by construction.

# Project Settings → API. Do not use the literal "your-project" hostname:
# lib/supabase.ts throws on it rather than failing mysteriously at runtime.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# Used for links in transactional email and for the payment callback URL.
VITE_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.com

# =============================================================================
# SERVER SECRETS — Supabase Edge Functions
# =============================================================================
# These must NEVER appear in this file with a VITE_ prefix, and should not be
# kept in .env at all. Set them with:
#
#   supabase secrets set NAME=value
#
# or in Dashboard → Project Settings → Edge Functions → Secrets.
#
#   RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxx
#     Resend API key. Rotate it if it has ever been committed or shared.
#
#   RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=The Security Watch <noreply@your-verified-domain.com>
#     Must be a domain verified in Resend. The onboarding@resend.dev sender only
#     delivers to the Resend account owner, so production email silently fails
#     for everyone else.
#
#   SEND_EMAIL_HOOK_SECRET=v1,whsec_xxxxxxxx
#     Auth → Hooks → Send Email → signing secret. The auth-send-email function
#     REJECTS any request whose signature does not verify — if auth emails stop
#     arriving, this value is the first thing to check.
#
#   PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_xxxxxxxx
#     Server-side only. Used to initialize transactions and to verify the
#     webhook HMAC. A payment can only be marked completed by that webhook.
#
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://thesecuritywatch.com,https://www.thesecuritywatch.com
#     Comma-separated CORS allowlist for the edge functions. localhost is
#     permitted automatically for development.
#
#   SITE_URL=https://thesecuritywatch.com
#     Where Paystack returns the payer after checkout, and the host used for
#     links in reminder emails.
#
#   PAYMENT_REMINDER_SECRET=<openssl rand -hex 32>
#     Authenticates the payment-reminders sweep, sent as x-sweep-secret. The
#     function refuses to run if this is unset rather than sweeping open — an
#     unauthenticated caller could otherwise burn every payer's reminder
#     cadence in one loop, and the ledger would record those nudges as sent.
#     See also PUSH_DISPATCH_SECRET and CUSTODIAN_SWEEP_SECRET, same shape.
#
# Supplied automatically by the platform — do not set these yourself:
#   SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY

# =============================================================================
# NOT USED
# =============================================================================
# Stripe is not implemented. The public pricing page and FAQ no longer claim it.
# If it is added later, the secret key belongs in Edge Function secrets and the
# integration must follow the same shape as Paystack: server-side
# initialization, webhook-verified settlement, no client-side status writes.
